{"id":"8bf8017544705588f0012561f4f79a161f79fd7d","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"8bf8017544705588f0012561f4f79a161f79fd7d","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"rust/AGENTS.md","lines":["@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ Define each request invariant once (single source of truth), in the lowest layer"," - **Wire parsing (`serde`)**: JSON shape, field types, and closed wire enums. HTTP handlers take `Result<Json<T>, JsonRejection>` directly (which extracts `body.<path>` on data errors); do not add `validator` derive macros or duplicate bounds onto DTO structs."," - **Route boundary (`vllm-server` `validate.rs` / `convert.rs`)**: protocol-only invariants that lower crates do not see (such as `stream_options` requiring `stream`, `top_logprobs` requiring `logprobs`, or route-specific `metadata` limits), lowering-time format conversions, and server-state or per-route policy checks (`model_names.check`, `VLLM_MAX_N_SEQUENCES`). Keep temporary rejections of unimplemented fields isolated in `reject_unsupported_fields`."," - **Shared domain (`vllm-text` / `vllm-chat`)**: cross-route rules — sampling parameter bounds, `max_tokens >= 1`, `min_tokens <= max_tokens`, logprobs, stop strings (non-empty and `VLLM_MAX_STOP_STRINGS`), token IDs and vocab bounds, `cache_salt`, prompt length and truncation, chat messages, tools, templates, and multimodal limits.","-- **Fault classification and `param`**: `vllm_text::Error::kind()` and `vllm_chat::Error::kind()` classify every variant exhaustively into `ErrorKind::InvalidRequest { param }` or `ErrorKind::Internal`. Report the shared layer's canonical `param` name without per-protocol remapping, and leave `param` as `None` only for cross-field or non-field errors.","+- **Fault classification and `param`**: `vllm_text::Error::kind()` and `vllm_chat::Error::kind()` classify every variant exhaustively into `ErrorKind::InvalidRequest { param }` (HTTP 400, gRPC `INVALID_ARGUMENT`), `ErrorKind::Unavailable` (a request that cannot be taken now: HTTP 503, gRPC `UNAVAILABLE`) or `ErrorKind::Internal` (HTTP 500, gRPC `INTERNAL`). Each transport maps the kind once, wherever the error surfaces: preparation, submission or the output stream. Report the shared layer's canonical `param` name without per-protocol remapping, and leave `param` as `None` only for cross-field or non-field errors."," "," Upper stages may call the owner's check early to short-circuit before expensive work such as chat template rendering or outbound media fetches."," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/src/chat/src/error.rs","lines":["@@ -202,7 +202,8 @@ pub type Result<T> = std::result::Result<T, Error>;"," "," impl Error {","     /// Classify this error as a client request-validation failure (with its","-    /// canonical OpenAI `param`, if any) or an internal server failure.","+    /// canonical OpenAI `param`, if any), a request that cannot be taken now,","+    /// or an internal server failure.","     pub fn kind(&self) -> ErrorKind {","         match self {","             Self::Text(error) => error.kind(),","@@ -271,12 +272,6 @@ impl Error {","             }","         }","     }","-","-    /// Whether the request could not be taken now, so retrying later may","-    /// succeed.","-    pub fn is_unavailable(&self) -> bool {","-        matches!(self, Self::Text(error) if error.is_unavailable())","-    }"," }"," "," impl From<llm_multimodal::MediaConnectorError> for Error {"],"additions":2,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/src/server/src/error.rs","lines":["@@ -185,35 +185,35 @@ impl IntoResponse for ApiError {","     }"," }"," ","-/// Classify a text-pipeline submit failure: request validation failures are","-/// the client's fault and map to HTTP 400, mirroring the Python frontend. A","-/// request that cannot be taken now, such as one over a queue limit, maps to","-/// a retryable 503. Everything else stays an internal 500.","-pub fn text_submit_error(context: &'static str, error: vllm_text::Error) 